  "effectDecisions": [
    "All independently selectable lines retain their own source image and referents. No reference to Penny by name is added to an anonymous falcon line; Penny appears in the original later feedback. Czech sokolka follows the source-evidenced female falcon without naming her.",
    "The bridge poem retains collective past action, earth shaping, raging waters and the purpose of bringing friends together. Czech definite friends in context need no added possessive.",
    "The bug poem keeps the small busy insect, question about priorities and necessity of present work; the later WE-the-bugs joke retains plural participants.",
    "All27 actual source/target triples were read, including24 mixed groups. Keep source outcome identities even when a mixed poem happens to suggest a plausible image. No attempt to improve mixed endings.",
    "Oliver good-drink poem keeps plural friends, idle afternoon and first-person fortune. Repeated evaluative good is implicit in the positive fortune and pleasant gathering under the pinned poetry authority; the corrected last line changes I to shared we. Both quoted whole-poem occurrences agree.",
    "River poem preserves endless marching/journey/flow, and the complete water/time/glacier/rain/snow commentary.",
    "Adult poems preserve two ladies and singular equine stud, the flow from the rear down legs onto earth, Violet gentle lapping/cleaning Oliver own mess and renewed erection. No body role or giver/receiver swap. Silver-tongue is master-of-language followed by literal tongue callbacks."
  ],
